124
00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.700
♪ Your charger can’t tell where the power’s from: ♪

125
00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.880
♪ sun at noon, or wind at midnight. ♪

126
00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:10.760
♪ The outlet’s the interface. The plant’s the secret. ♪

127
00:08:11.967 --> 00:08:13.713
(narrator) The bridge, private isn’t enough.

128
00:08:13.713 --> 00:08:16.676
(narrator) Your hero thinks every field is private, so it’s hidden.

129
00:08:16.676 --> 00:08:25.353
(narrator) A code card shows the private fields, but the public checkout method returns a PayPalCharge and takes a PayPalAccount, all outlined in red: leaked in the signature.

130
00:08:25.353 --> 00:08:28.845
(narrator) Hiding data gets a stamp, not it; hiding decisions lights up gold.

131
00:08:28.845 --> 00:08:37.522
(narrator) Then a client and a server are joined by a visible contract, the server’s database choice stays hidden inside it, and stateless or stateful drops onto the contract.

132
00:08:38.127 --> 00:08:41.967
♪ “I made every field private. So it’s hidden, right?” ♪

133
00:08:42.107 --> 00:08:45.327
